### Question 9: `openCreateModal()` Pattern + `SnippetEditorModal.result` + Command Registration

#### 1. `SnippetManagerView.openCreateModal()` — The Reference Pattern (`src/views/snippet-manager-view.ts:258-267`)

```typescript
// src/views/snippet-manager-view.ts:258-267
private async openCreateModal(folderPath: string): Promise<void> {
  const modal = new SnippetEditorModal(this.app, this.plugin, {
    mode: 'create',
    initialFolder: folderPath,
  });
  modal.open();
  const result = await modal.result;
  if (result.saved) {
    await this.rebuildTreeModel();
    this.renderTree();
  }
}
```

The flow is:
1. Construct `SnippetEditorModal` with `mode: 'create'` and `initialFolder`.
2. Call `modal.open()` — this triggers `onOpen()` asynchronously.
3. `await modal.result` — suspends until the user saves or cancels.
4. If `result.saved === true`, refresh the tree view (the SnippetManagerView owns the tree).

**The inline runner does NOT own a tree view**, so its post-save handler is simpler — it would only need to show a `Notice` confirmation (or do nothing, since `SnippetService.save()` at `src/snippets/snippet-service.ts:212-241` already writes the snippet to disk).

The `openEditModal()` pattern (`src/views/snippet-manager-view.ts:231-257`) is the edit-mode counterpart — it loads a snippet first, passes it as `options.snippet`, and uses `mode: 'edit'`:

```typescript
// src/views/snippet-manager-view.ts:241-247
const modal = new SnippetEditorModal(this.app, this.plugin, {
  mode: 'edit',
  initialFolder: dirname(path),
  snippet,
});
modal.open();
const result = await modal.result;
```

#### 2. `SnippetEditorResult` — Discriminated Union (`src/views/snippet-editor-modal.ts:28-30`)

```typescript
// src/views/snippet-editor-modal.ts:28-30
type SnippetEditorResult =
  | { saved: true; snippet: Snippet; movedFrom: string | null }
  | { saved: false; duplicatedTo?: string };
```

- `{ saved: true; snippet: Snippet; movedFrom: string | null }` — successful save. `movedFrom` is `null` on create (line 553), or the old path on move (line 613). `snippet` is the saved draft with its final path.
- `{ saved: false; duplicatedTo?: string }` — cancel or duplicate. On cancel via `handleCancel()` (`src/views/snippet-editor-modal.ts:629-633`), `duplicatedTo` is absent. On duplicate via `handleDuplicate()` (`src/views/snippet-editor-modal.ts:636-641`), `duplicatedTo` is the new duplicate's path.

#### 3. `result` Promise — Lifecycle (`src/views/snippet-editor-modal.ts:85-86, 144-146, 676-680`)

The promise is declared as a readonly field and initialized in the constructor:

```typescript
// src/views/snippet-editor-modal.ts:85-86
readonly result: Promise<SnippetEditorResult>;
private resolve!: (value: SnippetEditorResult) => void;

// src/views/snippet-editor-modal.ts:144-146
this.result = new Promise<SnippetEditorResult>((res) => {
  this.resolve = res;
});
```

It is resolved via `safeResolve()` (`src/views/snippet-editor-modal.ts:676-680`) — an idempotent wrapper that prevents double-resolution:

```typescript
// src/views/snippet-editor-modal.ts:676-680
private safeResolve(value: SnippetEditorResult): void {
  if (!this.resolved) {
    this.resolved = true;
    this.resolve(value);
  }
}
```

Resolution points:

| Location | Line | Value | Trigger |
|----------|------|-------|---------|
| Create save (simple) | 553 | `{ saved: true, snippet: draftToSave, movedFrom: null }` | `handleSave()` — no folder/name change |
| Edit save (move/rename) | 613 | `{ saved: true, snippet: finalDraft, movedFrom: oldPath }` | `handleSave()` — folder or name changed |
| Cancel (no unsaved) | 632 | `{ saved: false }` | `handleCancel()` — `super.close()` follows at 633 |
| Discard from guard | 670 | `{ saved: false }` | `runUnsavedGuard()` — discard branch |
| Duplicate | 640 | `{ saved: false, duplicatedTo: newPath }` | `handleDuplicate()` |
| `onClose()` | 239 | `{ saved: false }` | `onClose()` — safety net for any unhandled close |

After `safeResolve({ saved: true, ... })`, `super.close()` is called at `src/views/snippet-editor-modal.ts:554` (create) or `:614` (edit). The `close()` override at lines 256-264 intercepts for the unsaved-changes guard — if `hasUnsavedChanges` and not yet resolved, it runs `runUnsavedGuard()` instead of closing immediately.

**For the inline runner's create flow**, the key resolution is at line 553: `safeResolve({ saved: true, snippet: draftToSave, movedFrom: null })` followed by `super.close()`. The snippet is already on disk via `SnippetService.save()` at line 552. The runner's `await modal.result` will receive `{ saved: true, snippet, movedFrom: null }` — it can then optionally `new Notice(...)` and continue running.

#### 4. `SnippetService.save()` — Disk Persistence (`src/snippets/snippet-service.ts:212-241`)

```typescript
// src/snippets/snippet-service.ts:212-241
async save(snippet: Snippet): Promise<void> {
  const normalized = this.assertInsideRoot(snippet.path);  // ← safety: path must be under snippetFolderPath
  if (normalized === null) {
    throw new Error(`[RadiProtocol] save rejected unsafe path: ${snippet.path}`);
  }
  await this.mutex.runExclusive(normalized, async () => {
    await ensureFolderPath(this.app.vault, this.settings.snippetFolderPath);
    // ... parent folder creation ...
    let payload: string;
    if (snippet.kind === 'json') { ... }
    else if (snippet.kind === 'md-template') {
      payload = serializeMarkdownTemplate(snippet);  // ← md-template serialization
    } else { ... }
    const exists = await this.app.vault.adapter.exists(normalized);
    if (exists) { await this.app.vault.adapter.write(normalized, payload); }
    else { await this.app.vault.create(normalized, payload); }
  });
}
```

This confirms the snippet is fully persisted to the vault filesystem before `safeResolve` fires. The runner's create flow needs no additional save logic — the modal handles it all.

